  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "Australia declared war on birds and lost. November 1932, Western Australia, and the enemy was twenty thousand emus.",
        "visual_query": "australian wheat field outback",
        "visual_fallback": "dry farmland"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The birds were flattening wheat that soldier-settlers had been given after the First World War. The farmers asked for machine guns.",
        "visual_query": "vintage australian farm harvest",
        "visual_fallback": "wheat harvest"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They got them. Two Lewis guns, ten thousand rounds, and a major to run the operation.",
        "visual_query": "historic military machine gun",
        "visual_fallback": "old army equipment"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Emus do not stand still. They split into small groups, ran at fifty kilometres an hour, and absorbed hits that should have dropped them.",
        "visual_query": "emu running grassland australia",
        "visual_fallback": "running birds"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The final count was under a thousand birds for nearly ten thousand rounds. The operation was quietly dropped and fences were built instead.",
        "visual_query": "wire fence outback boundary",
        "visual_fallback": "farm fence"
      }
    ],
